Maximum XOR Subarray

You already have:

✅ Maximum XOR of two numbers
❌ But NOT Maximum XOR of a subarray

This one is very powerful — frequently asked in product companies.

✅ Problem Statement

Given an integer array arr[], find the maximum XOR value of any subarray.

A subarray must be continuous.

🧩 Example
Input:
arr = [8, 1, 2, 12]

Output:
15

Why?

Subarray:

1 ^ 2 ^ 12 = 15


That’s the maximum possible XOR.

⚠️ Brute Force Approach

Compute XOR for every subarray.

Time Complexity:

O(N²)


Not optimal.

🧠 Optimized Approach (INTERVIEW LEVEL)

We use:

✅ Prefix XOR
✅ Bitwise Trie

🔥 Key Mathematical Insight

Let:

prefix[i] = arr[0] ^ arr[1] ^ ... ^ arr[i]


Then:

XOR of subarray (i+1 to j)
= prefix[j] ^ prefix[i]


So instead of computing subarray XOR repeatedly:

We convert problem to:

👉 Find two prefix XOR values whose XOR is maximum.

🧠 Why Trie?

If we maximize:

prefix[j] ^ prefix[i]


We want opposite bits at each position.

Trie helps us:

Store prefix values in binary

Greedily choose best opposite bit

🪜 Step-by-Step Algorithm

Initialize Trie

Insert 0 into Trie (important)

Maintain prefixXor

For each element:

prefixXor ^= element

Query trie for best XOR

Insert prefixXor into trie

Return maximum

⏱ Time Complexity

Each number → 32 bits

For N numbers:

O(32N) ≈ O(N)


Very efficient.

☕ Java Implementation
🔹 Step 1: Trie Node
class TrieNode {
    TrieNode[] children = new TrieNode[2];

    TrieNode() {
        children[0] = null;
        children[1] = null;
    }
}

Explanation

Each node has:

children[0] → bit 0

children[1] → bit 1

Since numbers are binary.

🔹 Step 2: Main Solution
class Solution {

    TrieNode root = new TrieNode();


Root of Trie.

🔹 Step 3: Insert Method
    void insert(int num) {
        TrieNode node = root;

        for (int i = 31; i >= 0; i--) {
            int bit = (num >> i) & 1;

            if (node.children[bit] == null) {
                node.children[bit] = new TrieNode();
            }

            node = node.children[bit];
        }
    }

🔍 Line-by-Line
for (int i = 31; i >= 0; i--)


We check 32 bits (integer).

(num >> i) & 1


Extract ith bit.

if node.children[bit] == null
    create node


Insert into Trie.

🔹 Step 4: Query Method (Important)
    int query(int num) {
        TrieNode node = root;
        int maxXor = 0;

        for (int i = 31; i >= 0; i--) {
            int bit = (num >> i) & 1;
            int opposite = 1 - bit;

            if (node.children[opposite] != null) {
                maxXor |= (1 << i);
                node = node.children[opposite];
            } else {
                node = node.children[bit];
            }
        }

        return maxXor;
    }

🔍 Line-by-Line Explanation
opposite = 1 - bit


To maximize XOR:
If current bit is 1 → we want 0
If current bit is 0 → we want 1

if opposite exists
    choose that


Because:

1 ^ 0 = 1
0 ^ 1 = 1


That gives maximum contribution.

maxXor |= (1 << i)


Set ith bit in result.

🔹 Step 5: Main Function
    public int maxSubarrayXOR(int[] arr) {

        insert(0);  // Important
        int prefix = 0;
        int result = 0;

        for (int num : arr) {

            prefix ^= num;

            result = Math.max(result, query(prefix));

            insert(prefix);
        }

        return result;
    }
}

🔥 Why Insert(0) Initially?

Because:

Subarray starting from index 0:

prefix[j] ^ 0 = prefix[j]


So we must insert 0.

